// Exeter armurer — Smythen Street, c. 1300.
// Sources: Statute of Winchester (1285) arming-tier requirements
// drove demand for fitted mail / brigandine / great-helm in
// boroughs; Exeter Mayor's Court Rolls 1300-1310 (Devon Heritage
// Centre, Exeter ECC ED/M/CR/1-3) record "armurer" surnames
// clustering on Smythen St. (the smiths' lane running south from
// High St. — name attested in Hooker's 1587 map and earlier
// civic deeds). Stone-walled because a serious arms forge needed
// thicker thermal mass + fire defence than a domestic hearth, and
// armurer guild status came with the means to build in stone.
// Forge / anvil / armour-rack furniture is deferred to Card 3.
Prefab(
    tag: "smithy",
    tier: Urban,
    variant: "armorer",
    weight: 3,
    size: (7, 7),
    palette: {
        '#': StoneWall,
        '.': Floor,
        'o': CobbleRoad,
    },
    grid: [
        "#######",
        "#.....#",
        "#.....#",
        "#.....o",
        "#.....#",
        "#.....#",
        "#######",
    ],
)
